@startuml training-tuning-loop
' The hyperparameter search loop, expressed in terms of the commands that
' actually implement each step. Held-out perplexity is the objective; the
' train/dev/test split discipline is what keeps the reported number honest. The
' loop distinguishes the two cost classes: re-fitting an expert (expensive - one
' corpus pass per candidate) from re-assembling a hybrid (cheap - no corpus pass
' at all), which is why alpha and strategy are the cheapest knobs to sweep.
' Render: plantuml -tsvg docs/diagrams/training-tuning-loop.puml
' Source of truth for Figure 1 in docs/training/hyperparameters.md §2.
skinparam backgroundColor #FAFAFA
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam rectangle {
  FontColor white
  FontStyle bold
  BorderColor #263238
  roundCorner 12
}
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #ECEFF1
  BorderColor #546E7A
  FontColor #263238
}
skinparam ArrowColor #37474F
skinparam ArrowFontColor #37474F
title Hyperparameter tuning — a held-out perplexity loop

rectangle "**Corpus**" as corpus #455A64
rectangle "**Split**\ntrain 80% · dev 10% · test 10%" as split #546E7A
rectangle "**train.txt**\nfits the parameters" as train #455A64
rectangle "**dev.txt**\nselects the hyperparameters" as dev #455A64
rectangle "**test.txt**\nreported once, at the very end" as test #455A64

rectangle "**Candidate θ**\norder · min-count · dim · window\nepochs · neg-samples · α · strategy" as cand #6A1B9A

rectangle "**Expensive arm**\n""train ngram"" / ""train embedding""\n**one corpus pass per candidate**" as fit #1565C0
rectangle "**Cheap arm**\n""train hybrid""\n**re-assembly only — no corpus pass**" as assemble #1B6CA8

rectangle "**eval perplexity**\n⟨MODEL⟩ dev.txt" as evaluate #546E7A
rectangle "**PPL(θ)**\nexp(−(1/N)·Σ log ℙ)" as score #6A1B9A
rectangle "**θ\* = argmin PPL**" as best #6A1B9A
rectangle "**eval perplexity**\n⟨MODEL⟩ test.txt\nthe unbiased number" as final #546E7A

corpus --> split
split --> train
split --> dev
split --> test

cand --> fit : order / dim / window /\nepochs / min-count changed
cand --> assemble : only α or strategy changed
train --> fit
fit --> assemble : ngram.bin + embed.bin
assemble --> evaluate
dev --> evaluate
evaluate --> score
score --> cand : next candidate
score --> best : grid exhausted
best --> final
test --> final

note right of assemble
  Sweeping **α** or **""--strategy""** never touches the
  corpus: hold the two experts fixed and re-assemble.
  A whole α grid costs one model load, not one
  training run per point.
end note

note bottom of score
  Compare candidates on **dev** only. Touch **test** once,
  after θ\* is frozen — otherwise the reported perplexity
  is a selection artefact rather than a measurement.
end note

@enduml
